  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The impact of the Covid-19 pandemic on the mental health of workers in health services: building resilience in post-conflict territories</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Deliver significant research funding for internationally competitive and innovative collaborative projects between researchers from Colombia and United Kingdom that will allow the pursuit of shared research interests.
The ODA statement says: We expect that this research will impact the mental health of health workers during and in the post-pandemic. We will use this information to impact decision making through our  interaction with policymakers and local institutions. We expect that improvements in the  mental health of health worker will benefit the quality of the health services. As a result of  better services, we will have improved health and improve socio-economic development. 
Furthermore, the project will contribute to reducing the impacts of violence on mental health because we plan to study the interaction between the stressor associated with the pandemic and the history of violence. We consider that this knowledge will help policymakers to  prioritized mental health services.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The fund addresses the UN sustainable development goals. It aims to maximise the impact of research and innovation to improve lives and opportunity in the developing world</narrative>
  </description>
